{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Everything</b> — Rabbi Judah said: Because the instrumentalist produces melodies on the lyre, and the melodies vary according to the length of the breath and the shortness of the voice, or its height or lowness or its swiftness, therefore he concluded with 'everything that has breath, praise YH.' And Rabbi Solomon the Sephardi said: For this is a hint to the supernal soul that is in the heavens. See the Book of Praises, complete and finished. And Abraham his son gathered them all: 'And the praises of El have not ended forever, and who is he that began and concluded them.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 150, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:15.729467592Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}